# ── Reference material (not source) ─────────────────────────
# Full-page screenshots of the live site, kept locally for comparison.
reference ss/

# Scrape + tooling artifacts: scraped WordPress HTML/CSS, generated
# screenshots and throwaway puppeteer scripts (~15MB). Local only.
scratch/

# ── Not part of the shipped site ────────────────────────────
# Alternative redesign build — kept on disk for reference, not shipped.
src/_redesign/

# public/media/ used to be ignored as "generated WebP derivatives", on the
# reasoning that the site served originals from public/images/. That stopped
# being true: src/ now references 25 files under /media/ and only 3 under
# /images/, so the rule was shipping a repo whose every image 404s on a fresh
# clone. The WebPs are the source assets now and belong in the repo (~1MB).
